cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this proof or checker, cite this archive and the sources listed in README.md."
title: "Two-bit shares for weakly private near-unanimous secret sharing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "An explicit perfectly correct near-unanimous threshold sharing construction for a one-bit secret, with two-bit shares and one-third weak privacy for all n at least four, answers the sublogarithmic-share question of Beimel, Ishai, Kushilevitz, and Li. Includes proof, limitations, and exact reproducibility checks."
